  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far (config_019, acc=0.639) uses multimodal + multiprofile + pca_n2000 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted. Key learned principles: multiprofile >> singleprofile, avgpool > transformer, weighted > concat, and multimodal > unimodal. However, the image modality has only been tested with resnet50, which scored very poorly in isolation (0.208). The most important untested variable in the current best pipeline is the image encoder quality. Question: Does upgrading to imagenet_vit_l (a substantially larger, more expressive encoder) provide complementary spatial/morphological signal that resnet50 could not capture, thereby pushing multimodal performance beyond 0.639? Why this is the best next experiment: It is a direct, single-variable extension of the best-performing config, keeping all proven-optimal settings fixed while testing the one major unknown. A positive result would validate further investment in the image branch; a null result would efficiently rule out the image encoder as a bottleneck and redirect budget toward other dimensions (e.g., RNA encoder or aggregation). This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

